## Hornero Chromatic (RFC 0002)

- `libs/chromatic/`, `plugin/src/Hornero/Chromatic/` and `extras/chromatic/`
  are a new implementation written for HorneroOS (GPL-3.0-only, like the
  rest of the runtime).
- **OKLab / OKLCH**: Björn Ottosson, "A perceptual color space for image
  processing" (2020), <https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/>; the
  published conversion matrices (MIT License) are used as constants.
- **WCAG 2.x** relative luminance and contrast ratio (W3C); **CIE76** ΔE on
  CIELAB D65; **median cut** (Heckbert, 1982) and **Lloyd's k-means** are
  textbook algorithms.
- **Feature lineage**: wallpaper seeds, variants, surface depth, smart
  mode/variant inference and app templates follow the ideas of
  [Caelestia](https://github.com/caelestia-dots) (shell and cli, GPL-3.0).
  No Caelestia code or tables were copied; Chromatic produces Hornero
  Signal roles directly and uses no external colour library.

